quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  10,43,And among them are those who look at you. But can you show the way to the blind even if they do not see?
  10,44,"Allah does not wrong people in the least; instead, it is the people who wrong themselves."
  10,45,"On the Day when He will gather them, (it will be) as if they had stayed (in the world) no longer than a single hour of a day, getting to recognise one another. Lost indeed will be the ones who deny the meeting with Allah and are not (rightly) guided."
  10,46,"Whether We show you a part (of the punishment) We have threatened them with, or We cause you to die (before that), yet their return shall be to Us. Then Allah (Himself) will be witness to what they do."
  10,47,"For every community, there is a messenger. After their messenger has come, judgement is passed between them in all fairness. And (similarly) they shall not be wronged (in the Hereafter)."
  10,48,And they say: ‘When will this warning (of punishment) be fulfilled if you are truthful?’
  10,49,"Say: ‘I do not own for myself (protection from) any harm, nor any benefit, except what Allah intends. There is an appointed term for every community. When their term arrives, they can not delay it by a moment, nor can they advance it.’*"
  10,50,"Say: ‘(O disbelievers,) have you considered, if His punishment overtakes you by night or by day, what part of it the wicked would seek to hasten?’"
  10,51,"What! When it happens, (only) then will you believe it? (It will be said:) ‘Now? While you would seek to hasten it (before)?"
  10,52,Then the wrongdoers will be told: ‘Taste the punishment of eternity. Should you be recompensed except for what you used to earn?’
  10,53,"They ask you (O Prophet): ‘Is it true?’ Say: ‘Yes! By my Lord, it is true. And you cannot escape it.’"
